# Worker Process (Mandatory)

`docs/ops/WORKER.md` is the operational execution contract. Read it before any
implementation work.

## Protocol

```text
READ docs/ops/WORKER.md
 -> Understand current phase
 -> Inspect relevant files
 -> STOP
 -> ASK USER FOR APPROVAL
 -> Implement ONLY the approved phase
 -> Run validation
 -> Update docs/ops/WORKER.md
 -> Report result
 -> STOP
```

## Status model

`PENDING` | `READY` | `IN_PROGRESS` | `BLOCKED` | `COMPLETED`

- Only **one** phase may be `IN_PROGRESS`.
- Never mark a phase `COMPLETED` unless its validation criteria pass.
- Never silently begin the next phase. After completion: set next phase to `PENDING`/`READY`,
  STOP, and ask for approval.

## After completing a phase

1. Update `docs/ops/WORKER.md` (tasks checked, changed files, validation results, issues,
   decisions).
2. Set the next phase appropriately.
3. Report and STOP.

## Scope control

- Modify only the approved phase scope.
- If an unrelated problem is found: document it in `docs/ops/WORKER.md` Backlog; do not
  silently fix it.
- Do not install dependencies, create apps/packages, or rewrite source unless the approved phase
 explicitly requires it.

## Agent roster (ad-hoc work)

For Cursor chat roles (Coordinator / Dizayner / Worker / İcraçı), build/git/deploy ownership,
and Agent Report format: see `coordinator-agent.mdc`, `icraciAgent.mdc`, and
`docs/ops/WORKER.md` §4a–§4b. Phase protocol above still applies to numbered roadmap phases.
Academy LMS track uses §4b checkpoint (İcraçı) and must not be mixed with numbered monorepo
phases.

## Current expectation until Phase 1 is approved

Phase 1 (Monorepo Foundation) remains `PENDING` until the user explicitly approves it.
